Comments about OPENDLG


OPENDLG is a dll which is copied to the ..\dll directory.  Programs
which use OPENDLG will need the files OPENDLG.LIB and OPENDLG.H. This
is taken care of in the make files of the samples that use OPENDLG.

OPENDLG contains the code for two dialog boxes, one for opening files
for reading, and the other for opening/creating files for writing (saving).
These dialogs shoud not be used for new samples, as they are replaced
by standard system dialogs in OS/2 2.0.  Refer to the TEMPLATE sample
for the use of standard dialogs.

HELLO is a sample app which illustrates each kind of dialog box.  This
sample is in the HELLO subdirectory; to run it type HELLO\HELLO.
